      "Shanawdithit was captured with her mother and sister in 1823 and lived as a servant in a settler household. In the last months of her life, she drew maps and pictures of Beothuk life for a man named William Cormack, who was trying to record what was known about her people. Her drawings are among the few records of Beothuk culture. She died of tuberculosis in 1829, and the Beothuk are remembered as one of the great tragedies of North American history.",
